Title: Multi-Fidelity Data-Based Optimization Algorithms
Version: 1.0-0
Date: 2026-09-29
Author: Wenje Ma
Maintainer: Wenje Ma <you@example.com>
Description: Standalone R scripts implementing a budget-constrained
  multi-fidelity Bayesian optimization pipeline based on the report in
  tex/report_v1.qmd. The pipeline builds a nested maximum-projection
  design for the low- and high-fidelity evaluations, optionally screens
  inactive parameters with a maximum one-factor-at-a-time (MOFAT)
  design, fits a Kennedy-O'Hagan auto-regressive fusion of the two
  fidelity levels, and then adds points one at a time by Expected
  Improvement until the high-fidelity budget is exhausted. Four
  benchmark problems are provided in 1, 2, 4, and 8 dimensions (Joseph
  1-D, Branin, an additive problem, and the borehole model), each with
  an accurate high-fidelity function and a cheap biassed low-fidelity
  version. Two experiments are included: a calibration sweep over the
  number of high-fidelity points n2 and an ablation study that isolates
  the contribution of the screening and fusion components across four
  configurations.
Imports: lhs, SFDesign, MOFAT, rkriging
